        "args": {
          "content": "{\n  \"module\": \"plugins/scaffolder-react\",\n  \"verdict\": \"needs_changes\",\n  \"tool_calls\": 34,\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"file\": \"plugins/scaffolder-react/src/next/lib/schema.ts\",\n      \"line\": 505,\n      \"issue\": \"In `resolveDependencyObject` (lines 505-540) and root `anyOf` in `resolveSchemaNode` (lines 692-763), when a `oneOf`/`anyOf` branch has no discriminator properties (`discriminatorKeys.size === 0`), `buildBranchTestSchema` (lines 322-346) adds `anyOf: propKeys.map(key => ({ required: [key] }))`. When the user has not yet filled the dependent field in `formData`, `validator.isValid` returns `false`, and because `resolveDependencyObject` (and root `anyOf`) lacks the `!matched && firstDiscriminatorKeys.size === 0` fallback that root `oneOf` has at lines 744-761, the branch is dropped and its fields are wrongly hidden. Reproducer: `resolveStepSchema({ type: 'object', dependencies: { foo: { oneOf: [{ properties: { artifact: { type: 'string' } } }] } } }, { foo: 'value' }, { previousStepKeys: new Set(['foo']) })` (from `ReviewState/util.test.ts:127`) or `resolveStepSchema({ type: 'object', anyOf: [{ properties: { anyOfField: { type: 'string' } } }] }, {}, { resolveAll: true })` returns `{ type: 'object' }` with `artifact` / `anyOfField` missing.\",\n      \"fix\": \"In `resolveDependencyObject` (for `oneOf` and `anyOf`) and in `resolveSchemaNode` step 4 (for `anyOf` as well as `oneOf`), fall back to merging `firstObjectBranch` when `!matched && firstObjectBranch && firstDiscriminatorKeys?.size === 0` (matching RJSF's `getFirstMatchingOption` fallback to option 0).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"file\": \"plugins/scaffolder-react/src/next/lib/schema.ts\",\n      \"line\": 322,\n      \"issue\": \"In `buildBranchTestSchema` (lines 322-346), when constructing `testSchema` for a non-discriminator `oneOf`/`anyOf` branch via `{ ...branch, anyOf: anyOfReq }`, spreading `...branch` preserves `branch.required` at the top level of `testSchema`."
        },
        "canonical_path": null,
